# onnxruntime-node fetches its CUDA execution provider from GitHub at install
# time. Its script assumes CUDA 12 on Linux/x64 even when nvcc is missing, and
# the tarball it asks for is not published for the version this tree resolves
# (the URL it requests returns 404), so a plain `npm install` / `npm ci` on Linux
# died before anything was built.
#
# The CPU runtime the app uses ships inside the package, so the CUDA fetch is
# off by default. A machine that wants the CUDA provider installs it on purpose
# from Microsoft's PyPI wheel instead of that dead URL, with
#
#   npm run setup:cuda
#
# and the app only asks for it when launched with BSP_WHISPER_DEVICE=cuda. See
# the README section "CUDA execution provider" before running either: the
# installer's own ONNXRUNTIME_NODE_INSTALL_CUDA switch still reaches the 404.
onnxruntime-node-install-cuda=skip
